+++ b/compat/v015/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# v0.1.5 metadata compatibility contract
+
+`testdata/legacy.json` is synthetic metadata using the JSON tags and nested raw
+resource shapes reviewed in `types/workload.go`, `types/node.go`,
+`resource/types/resource.go`, and the store key layout at upstream v0.1.5
+commit `e19ceb7e09d95bedea3eb0c25bec9308101fecc5`. It is not a live export or a
+claim that an older binary generated this exact fixture.
+
+The tests exercise real core store update/delete/status binding and RPC
+conversion. Only the KV transport and cluster retrieval boundary are fixtures.
+They assert exact workload identity and owner/digest labels, persisted resource
+round trips, fenced node identity, RPC resource capacity/usage preservation,
+exact four-key cleanup with unrelated data preserved, and missing status that
+must never inherit a neighboring node's readiness. Metadata cleanup deliberately
+does not claim to repair external resource-plugin quota.
+
+The error migration is intentional: v0.1.5 classified an empty etcd exact read
+as invalid cardinality and returned the custom GetWorkload RPC code. v0.1.7
+must distinguish empty reads (`ErrKeyNotFound` / workload `NotFound`) from
+ambiguous counts and backend failures. Narrow no-network tests alongside the
+etcd meta package exercise the actual GetOne/GetMulti implementation and reject
+partial results when one exact key is absent or ambiguous.
+
+Run both parts against the patched candidate:
+
+```sh
+go test ./compat/v015 -count=1 -v
+go test ./store/etcdv3/meta -run '^TestV015' -count=1 -v
+```
+
+These are bounded metadata/wire compatibility tests. They do not establish
+plugin accounting, rolling upgrade, live runtime, network, or VPS compatibility.
+A compile failure or either command failing blocks publication; do not replace
+this evidence with unrelated package tests or alter upstream code silently.
